  "question": {
    "text": "The elevation in boiling point for <math><mn>1</mn></math> molal solution of glucose is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The depression in freezing point for <math><mn>2</mn></math> molal solution of glucose in the same solvent is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2&#160;</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The relation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub></math> is:"
  },
